## 6️⃣ Now about `verify()` — how it REALLY works

### This line in your test:

```java
verify(historyRepository).save(any());
```

Means:

> “Assert that `save()` was called **at least once** with any argument.”

Mockito internally tracks:

* Which methods were called
* How many times
* With what arguments

---

### 🔹 Verify exact call count

```java
verify(historyRepository, times(1)).save(any());
```

Other options:

```java
times(n)
never()
atLeastOnce()
atMost(2)
```

---

### 🔹 Verify exact argument

```java
verify(historyRepository).save(
    argThat(history ->
        history.getAction().equals("FORWARD") &&
        history.getProbeId().equals(1L)
    )
);
```

This is **very powerful**.

---

## 7️⃣ Order verification (advanced, optional)

```java
InOrder inOrder = inOrder(remoteSeaProbeService, historyRepository);

inOrder.verify(remoteSeaProbeService).getProbeEntity(1L);
inOrder.verify(historyRepository).save(any());
```

Use this when **sequence matters**.

